# IT57: exact BEFORE and AFTER wording of the two investigation cells (English source). Written before any reader ran.
BEFORE_INV04 = "The same provoked-seizure design with both genotypes treated and an interaction term, powered on the published effect size."
ADD_INV04 = (" [IT57; ADV-051, ADV-054, ADV-059, ADV-061] The published effect size cannot be used to power it: the paper reports no genotype-by-treatment test, does not state the age of the pups, "
 "and its wild-type pups sit near the floor of the scale; from its curves the variability of the 60-minute summary is a bracket (a coefficient of variation of about 0.6 to 1.2 in knockouts, read from means and error bars, not a value), "
 "which puts the interaction contrast at about 180 to 320 animals per cell at the paper's stimulus, so a pilot comes first and fixes the variability, the assay age and a stimulus that gives wild type a measurable response. "
 "The design also needs: wild-type pups at the assay age and at two or more older ages; reference agents with different age profiles as an assay-sensitivity panel (the rat age floor for this agent is an inference, unresolved for the mouse); "
 "seizure type recorded per animal and a motor control; a dose check at each age; and a selective T-type blocker beside this agent, because no T-type current has been measured in any WWOX system (the held transcript sets do not sample the thalamus) and the cell pharmacology of this agent is contested. "
 "The margin for the same size is the interaction ratio (the knockout effect ratio over the wild-type effect ratio, on the log scale): genotype-specific if at most 0.7 or at least 1.43, not genotype-specific between 0.7 and 1.43, fixed before data (in vivo brief, section 2.7).")
AFTER_INV04 = BEFORE_INV04 + ADD_INV04
ADD_INV09 = (" [IT57; ADV-051, ADV-059] In the same assay the lithium regimen (a single against a repeated pretreatment) is a design variable that can change the sign in one family of mouse provoked-seizure papers; "
 "the one experiment held shows an effect in all three genotypes, which is more consistent with a general effect than a knockout-specific one, so reading a genotype effect needs a general anticonvulsant comparator that does not act on this kinase, "
 "an age series in wild-type pups, and a second inhibitor of another class as the attribution control.")
